 "_comment": "Temporary-visa share of full-time S&E&H graduate enrolment (GSS 2024) joined to federal research and development expenditures (HERD FY2024 table 14). THE MONEY AND THE ENROLMENT SIT IN THE SAME INSTITUTIONS: by quartile of federal R&D, the doctoral visa share runs 20.5% in the lowest against 43.6% in the highest, and the highest quartile holds 167,396 of the doctoral students against 7,631 in the lowest. Master's runs 32.9% to 50.3%. ONE NUANCE THAT MUST BE KEPT: the very highest master's SHARES are at institutions with almost no federal R&D -- tuition-funded programmes -- so 'highest share' and 'most federal money' name different institutions even though the overall relationship is positive. MATCHING goes through the GSS UNITID to the IPEDS campus name, because HERD campus-qualifies its names and fourteen GSS names cover more than one campus -- matching on the GSS name alone collapsed Ann Arbor, Dearborn and Flint into one record. Names are then matched exactly on a normalised form; nothing is fuzzy-matched. UNMATCHED IS NOT ZERO: an institution may be absent from HERD, which does suggest little R&D, or its name may simply not have been recovered, and these cannot be told apart here. HERD reports R&D EXPENDITURE, not obligations or student support, and is not all federal money an institution receives. Enrolments, not degrees.",
